 * Maintenance work orders — the one door for their data and for everything that moves stock because of them.
 *
 *  - **Reporting / planning** a work order (a breakdown, a preventive job, a corrective job) for an active asset at a branch the person works in. A breakdown records when the asset
 *    **stopped**. The number is taken first, in the transaction. A checklist (one task per line) becomes the tasks to tick.
 *  - **Assigning** to an active technician who may do the work; **starting** (also done by the first tick, part or hours); **ticking tasks**; **issuing spare parts** (`StockService::issue`,
 *    once per entry, approved active items only); **logging hours**.
 *  - **Completing** needs every task ticked and a note; a breakdown records when the asset was **running again** (not before it stopped, not in the future) — downtime is worked out from
 *    the two. A preventive order moves its schedule on from the day it was done. **Cancelling** is only before any part was issued or hours logged.
 *  - **`generateDue()`** makes the preventive orders that have come due, once for each due date (`unique(plan, due date)`) and never while the schedule still has one open.
 *  - Every change takes the order's row lock first; every part and hours entry carries an `entry_key`, so a double click is one entry.
 */";s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀namespaceUses";O:30:"PHPStan\Analyser\NamespaceUses":3:{s:9:"namespace";s:32:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Services";s:4:"uses";a:20:{s:4:"user";s:15:"App\Models\User";s:18:"fieldruleexception";s:45:"App\Modules\CRM\Exceptions\FieldRuleException";s:14:"stockexception";s:47:"App\Modules\Inventory\Exceptions\StockException";s:5:"batch";s:34:"App\Modules\Inventory\Models\Batch";s:12:"stockservice";s:43:"App\Modules\Inventory\Services\StockService";s:12:"lossincident";s:36:"App\Modules\Loss\Models\LossIncident";s:5:"asset";s:36:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Models\Asset";s:17:"maintenancelabour";s:48:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Models\MaintenanceLabour";s:16:"maintenanceorder";s:47:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Models\MaintenanceOrder";s:15:"maintenancepart";s:46:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Models\MaintenancePart";s:15:"maintenanceplan";s:46:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Models\MaintenancePlan";s:15:"maintenancetask";s:46:"App\Modules\Maintenance\Models\MaintenanceTask";s:10:"itemlookup";s:39:"App\Modules\Masters\Services\ItemLookup";s:12:"documenttype";s:37:"App\Modules\Shared\Enums\DocumentType";s:19:"numberseriesservice";s:47:"App\Modules\Shared\Services\NumberSeriesService";s:13:"tenantcontext";s:40:"App\Modules\Shared\Tenancy\TenantContext";s:15:"carbonimmutable";s:22:"Carbon\CarbonImmutable";s:34:"uniqueconstraintviolationexception";s:54:"Illuminate\Database\UniqueConstraintViolationException";s:2:"db";s:29:"Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB";s:19:"validationexception";s:41:"Illuminate\Validation\ValidationException";}s:9:"constUses";a:0:{}}}s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀abstract";b:0;s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀final";b:1;s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀extends";N;s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀implements";a:0:{}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀usedTraits";a:0:{}s:70:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\E