 * Production orders — the one door for their data and for everything that moves stock because of them.
 *
 *  - **Making one** (draft): an approved, active bill of materials, a quantity, dates and a branch the person works in. The components it requires are **copied from the bill** then
 *    (quantity × planned ÷ the bill's output, plus the wastage), so a later change of the bill moves nothing already planned. The order number is taken first, in the transaction.
 *  - **Releasing** puts it on the shop floor; the bill and its items must still be approved and active. The first issue or output makes it *in progress*.
 *  - **Issuing material** takes a component out of stock at the order's branch (`StockService::issue`, once per entry), up to what is required plus the company's tolerance.
 *  - **Reporting output** receives the good units into stock — at the material cost that went in, spread over the good units made so far — and records rejects with a reason. Up to the
 *    planned quantity plus the tolerance. A batch-tracked item needs a batch number (and an expiry if it has one).
 *  - **Completing** needs output; short of the plan it needs a note. **Cancelling** is only before any material was issued.
 *  - Every issue and output carries an `entry_key` (made when the form opened), so a double click or a retried request is one entry. The order row is locked first for every change.
 */";s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀namespaceUses";O:30:"PHPStan\Analyser\NamespaceUses":3:{s:9:"namespace";s:31:"App\Modules\Production\Services";s:4:"uses";a:18:{s:4:"user";s:15:"App\Models\User";s:18:"fieldruleexception";s:45:"App\Modules\CRM\Exceptions\FieldRuleException";s:14:"stockexception";s:47:"App\Modules\Inventory\Exceptions\StockException";s:5:"batch";s:34:"App\Modules\Inventory\Models\Batch";s:12:"stockservice";s:43:"App\Modules\Inventory\Services\StockService";s:4:"item";s:31:"App\Modules\Masters\Models\Item";s:10:"itemlookup";s:39:"App\Modules\Masters\Services\ItemLookup";s:3:"bom";s:33:"App\Modules\Production\Models\Bom";s:19:"productioncomponent";s:49:"App\Modules\Production\Models\ProductionComponent";s:15:"productionissue";s:45:"App\Modules\Production\Models\ProductionIssue";s:15:"productionorder";s:45:"App\Modules\Production\Models\ProductionOrder";s:16:"productionoutput";s:46:"App\Modules\Production\Models\ProductionOutput";s:12:"documenttype";s:37:"App\Modules\Shared\Enums\DocumentType";s:8:"location";s:34:"App\Modules\Shared\Models\Location";s:19:"numberseriesservice";s:47:"App\Modules\Shared\Services\NumberSeriesService";s:13:"tenantcontext";s:40:"App\Modules\Shared\Tenancy\TenantContext";s:2:"db";s:29:"Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB";s:19:"validationexception";s:41:"Illuminate\Validation\ValidationException";}s:9:"constUses";a:0:{}}}s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀abstract";b:0;s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀final";b:1;s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀extends";N;s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀implements";a:0:{}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀usedTraits";a:0:{}s:70:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀traitUseAdaptations";a:0:{}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedClassNode␀statements";a:8:{i:0;O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode":11:{s:56:"␀PHPSta